  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user with the account sync on and two devices whose account lists are in a different order, I want a reconcile that changes nothing to write nothing, so that the iCloud Keychain item is not rewritten at every foreground on both devices.\n\n### What happens\n`AccountSyncMerge` keeps **this device's** order for the merged entries (`AccountSyncMerge.swift`, \"local order first, new accounts appended\"; LOT-173 spec \"Merge\": \"The local order is kept\"). Two devices holding the same accounts in a different order therefore each compute an envelope that differs from the item only by the order, and write it: 8 item writes in 4 rounds of reconciles in a probe, same on `dev-swift` before #1406.\n\nFound by the Fable adversarial review of #1406 (round 2, finding 5), out of that PR's scope (#1390 is about cookie-expiry refreshes).\n\n### Proposed fix\nThe copy's entries keep the copy's order (new keys appended); the device-only book keeps this device's order. Test (Linux, `HFRStorageTests`): two devices with `[x, y]` and `[y, x]`, repeated reconciles → `itemWritten == false` after the first.\n\n### Acceptance\n- A reconcile between devices that hold the same accounts in a different order writes nothing to the synchronizable item.\n- Each device keeps its own order.\n\nRefs #1390, #1406.",
